Subject: [PATCH] DV GL: GL windowing context and GUI compositing generated from GLES

The DV-patched GLES GBM context carries native output, mode switching
and the PQ GUI composite. Kodi's GL and GLES contexts differ only in
names, EGL setup and renderer registration, so the GL context is
generated from the GLES one by scripts/cb1-gl-winsys.py instead of
being ported by hand. Core profile GL has no client-side arrays, so the
GUI quad is streamed through buffers as Kodi's own GL context did.

The GL composite shader takes the GLES shader's LUT, PQ input and output
range interface, and the bridge builds on GL with the GL video filter
shaders.

The generated context uses the R580 HDR10 scanout helper, so it builds
for GL too, with Kodi's GL header.

